window.SEARCH_INDEX = [{"url":"index.html","page":"Introduction","section":"","text":"Decisium UI tests in plain English. No selectors. npm install -g decisium && decisium install decisium run checkout.feature # live: records checkout.cassette.json decisium run checkout.feature --record none # replay in CI: no model calls No selectors. A Step says what the user wants; Decisium finds the element. Record and replay. CI replays recorded Steps: fast, free, the same result every run. Code decides pass or fail , not the model. Built on cucumber-js and Playwright. Your config, formatters and step definitions keep working. Steps are resolved by Jev, TypeSafe's decision model. Getting started · Examples · How it works"},{"url":"getting-started.html","page":"Getting started","section":"","text":"Getting started Needs Node 22.18+ (or 23.6+)."},{"url":"getting-started.html#1-install","page":"Getting started","section":"1. Install","text":"npm install --save-dev decisium # or: npm install -g decisium npx decisium install # the Chromium build Decisium drives; --with-deps on Linux A per-project install pins the version, so CI replays with the version that recorded. These docs write decisium … ; per project, type npx decisium … ."},{"url":"getting-started.html#2-add-your-api-key","page":"Getting started","section":"2. Add your API key","text":"Live runs call Jev through the TypeSafe API. Replays need no key. echo 'TYPESAFE_API_KEY=...' >> .env decisium doctor # checks Node, Chromium and the key"},{"url":"getting-started.html#3-write-a-feature","page":"Getting started","section":"3. Write a feature","text":"# features/campaign.feature @url:http://localhost:3000 Feature: Campaigns Scenario: Schedule a campaign When I enter \"Autumn Sale\" as the campaign name And I set the activation period to 2 weeks And I schedule the campaign Then the campaign status should be \"Scheduled\" @url: is the start URL (a URL or a local HTML file). Each scenario starts in a fresh browser. Quote every value a Step types or a check compares. More: Writing Steps ."},{"url":"getting-started.html#4-run-it","page":"Getting started","section":"4. Run it","text":"decisium lint features/campaign.feature # no browser: how each Step will be read decisium run features/campaign.feature # live: writes campaign.cassette.json decisium run features/campaign.feature --record none # replay: no model calls Commit the cassette and replay it in CI . When a Step fails, see Troubleshooting ."},{"url":"getting-started.html#what-is-sent-to-jev","page":"Getting started","section":"What is sent to Jev","text":"Per request: the Step's text and a text snapshot of the page (roles, names, visible text, link URLs). No screenshots, cookies or network traffic. Secrets written as \"$NAME\" leave your machine only as the token. Replays send nothing. Decisium is MIT; Jev is TypeSafe's hosted service under its own terms."},{"url":"examples.html","page":"Example","section":"","text":"Example A real public shop. Save the feature and run it: decisium run saucedemo.feature # live: records saucedemo.cassette.json decisium run saucedemo.feature --record none # replay: no model calls"},{"url":"examples.html#saucedemo","page":"Example","section":"saucedemo.feature","text":"A shop: login, sorting, the cart and checkout. Source 1 @url:https://www.saucedemo.com/ 2 Feature: Sauce Demo shop (login, sorting, cart, checkout validation) 3 Demo credentials are listed on the login page. 4 5 Scenario: A locked out user cannot log in 6 When I try to log in as \"locked_out_user\" with password \"secret_sauce\" 7 Then the error should say \"Sorry, this user has been locked out.\" 8 9 Scenario: Sorting by price puts the cheapest product first 10 When I log in as \"standard_user\" with password \"secret_sauce\" 11 And I sort the products by \"Price (low to high)\" 12 Then the first product price should be \"$7.99\" 13 14 Scenario: The cart counts added products 15 When I log in as \"standard_user\" with password \"secret_sauce\" 16 And I add \"Sauce Labs Backpack\" to the cart 17 And I put \"Sauce Labs Bike Light\" in the cart 18 Then the cart badge should show \"2\" 19 20 Scenario: Checkout requires a first name, then completes 21 When I log in as \"standard_user\" with password \"secret_sauce\" 22 And I add \"Sauce Labs Backpack\" to the cart 23 And I open the cart 24 And I start the checkout 25 And I try to continue without filling in the form 26 Then the error should say \"First Name is required\" 27 When I enter \"Ada\" as first name, \"Lovelace\" as last name and \"10115\" as postal code 28 And I continue 29 Then the item total should be \"$29.99\" 30 When I finish the order 31 Then the confirmation should say \"Thank you for your order!\" 32"},{"url":"how-it-works.html","page":"How it works","section":"","text":"How it works page ──► list of elements ──► Jev picks one + an action ──► Playwright acts ──► page changed? repeat until done Read. Decisium reads the page as text: its accessibility tree (roles, names, visible text, states). Pick. Jev chooses from that list: which element, and how to use it (click, type, select, press a key…). It never writes code, selectors or values; a typed value always comes from the Step's quotes. Act. Playwright performs the action, Decisium reads the new page, and the loop repeats until the Step's task is done. I delete the campaign may open a menu first, then click Delete. Check. For a Then Step, Jev only picks the subject and the kind of check. Code compares the quoted value with the page. Refuse to guess. When the pick is unclear (two \"Save\" buttons), the Step fails as AMBIGUOUS instead of clicking one. Record. What each Step resolved to (role, name, container) goes into <feature>.cassette.json . The next run replays it without Jev; if that element is gone, the Step fails as UI_CHANGED . Steps Decisium recognises on its own ( I press Escape , I go back , I go to \"/settings\" ) skip the model. decisium run -v prints every page snapshot and answer."},{"url":"steps.html","page":"Writing Steps","section":"","text":"Writing Steps A Step is an action ( When , it changes the page) or a check ( Then , code verifies the page). Any wording works, in any language Jev reads ( # language: de ). decisium lint flags the wordings to avoid."},{"url":"steps.html#rules","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Rules","text":"One Step, one task , named by what the user wants: I save the draft , not I click the Save draft button . Quote exact values : what to type, the option to pick, the text a check expects. Name things as the page labels them : \"the error\", \"the status\", \"the calendar\". Say \"open\" to open. I search for \"Ada\" runs a search; it does not open a result. Secrets as \"$NAME\" , read from the environment or .env . No CSS or XPath. When no wording works, write a client step ."},{"url":"steps.html#actions","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Actions","text":"To Write Open a place I open the calendar · I open the \"Spring Sale\" campaign Go to a URL I go to \"/settings\" · I go back · I reload the page Type I enter \"Winter Sale\" as the campaign name Clear a field I clear the Search field Select I set the activation period to 2 weeks Do a task I schedule the campaign · I delete the campaign Submit a search I search for \"Ada\" and submit the search Try what the app refuses I try to schedule the campaign Toggle I accept the terms · I turn off dark mode · I uncheck \"Newsletter\" Press a key I press Escape · I open the command palette by pressing Ctrl+K Hover I hover over the help button Drag, slider I drag \"Fix bug\" to the Done list · I set the volume to \"75\" Double/right click I right-click report.pdf and choose \"Delete\" Scroll a panel I scroll down the Inbox until \"Message 15\" is shown Upload I upload \"notes.txt\" with the Attach file button (path relative to the feature) Download I export the contacts as CSV Clipboard I copy the invite link · I paste into the message box Dialogs I delete the \"Groceries\" note (confirms) · I start deleting the \"Ideas\" note but cancel Tabs I close the tab · I switch back to the previous tab Confirm with a specific control I publish the post, confirming with \"Publish now\" Inputs take ISO values: \"2026-10-20\" , \"14:30\" . iframes and open shadow roots work like the rest of the page."},{"url":"steps.html#checks","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Checks","text":"To check Write A value the campaign status should be \"Draft\" · the Email field should be \"ada@example.com\" An error the error should say \"Set an activation date before scheduling\" Text on the page \"Saved\" should appear Text in an area \"Winter Sale\" should appear in the calendar Absence \"Charles Babbage\" should not appear in the results A state the \"Schedule\" button should be disabled · \"Newsletter\" should be unchecked A tooltip the tooltip should say \"Opens the docs\" A download the downloaded file name should be \"contacts.csv\" The clipboard the copied text should be \"https://example.com/invite/7f3a\" A dialog the confirm should say \"Delete the Groceries note?\" An earlier value the campaign should appear in the calendar (after quoting \"Winter Sale\") States: disabled, enabled, checked, unchecked, expanded, collapsed, selected, pressed. A subjective check ( the article should be well written ) runs only with --judged and reports JUDGED_PASSED / JUDGED_FAILED ."},{"url":"steps.html#tables-doc-strings-unique-values","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Tables, doc strings, unique values","text":"When I fill in the new contact: | First name | Ada | | Last name | Lovelace | And I write the notes: \"\"\" Wrote the first program. \"\"\" And I create an agent named \"Autotest agent {{decisium.runId}}\" An action table runs one Step per row. A check table is matched to a table on the page by column header. {{decisium.runId}} is a random ID, the same for the whole run."},{"url":"steps.html#out-of-scope","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Out of scope","text":"Canvas, maps, captchas, 2FA codes and closed shadow roots. Use a test mode in the app or a client step ."},{"url":"configuration.html","page":"CLI and configuration","section":"","text":"CLI and configuration"},{"url":"configuration.html#commands","page":"CLI and configuration","section":"Commands","text":"Command Does decisium run <file.feature[:line]>... Runs features; :line runs one scenario. decisium step \"<step>\" --url <url> Runs one Step, no feature file. For trying a wording. decisium lint <file.feature>... No browser, no model: how each Step will be read, and wordings to avoid. decisium pin <file.feature:line> <n> Confirms candidate n of an AMBIGUOUS action. See Pin . decisium install [--with-deps] Downloads Chromium ( --with-deps : Linux system libraries too). decisium doctor [<file.feature>...] Checks Node, Chromium, the API key and the start URLs. Exit codes: 0 passed, 1 a scenario failed, 2 configuration or infrastructure error."},{"url":"configuration.html#run-flags","page":"CLI and configuration","section":"run flags","text":"Flag --url <url|file> Start URL; overrides @url: . --record new|none|all new (default): replay, record what is missing. none : replay only (CI). all : re-record everything. --parallel <n|auto> Run features in parallel workers. --headed Show the browser. --strict Fail checks that passed with low confidence. --judged Let Jev judge subjective checks. --format <name[:path]> Any cucumber formatter, e.g. junit:junit.xml . Repeatable. --import <file> Your step definitions or hooks. Repeatable. -p <profile> A cucumber profile. --no-agent-report Do not write report.md . -v , --debug Print every page snapshot and answer; show stack traces."},{"url":"configuration.html#options","page":"CLI and configuration","section":"Options","text":"decisium run loads your cucumber.{js,mjs,cjs,json,yaml} like cucumber-js does. Decisium options go in worldParameters.decisium : // cucumber.mjs export default { worldParameters: { decisium: { url: \"http://localhost:3000\", reportDir: \"e2e/runs\", checkTimeout: 10000 }, }, }; Option Default When to change url Start URL for features without @url: . record \"new\" \"none\" in CI. reportDir \"runs\" To match your CI artifact path. checkTimeout 5000 Slow page: ms a check waits for the expected state. actionTimeout 5000 Slow app: ms to wait for the page to settle after an action. maxTurns 8 Long flows in one Step (1–20). Or split the Step. confidence.target 0.5 How sure Jev must be of the element. Reword the Step first. confidence.answer 0.8 How sure Jev must be of other answers. Below 0.6 warns. states \"**/*.state.feature\" Where state files live. Also headed , judged , strict , verbose , debug , agentReport . Every option has a flag ( --check-timeout ) and an environment variable ( DECISIUM_CHECK_TIMEOUT ). Precedence: flag > environment > config file > default."},{"url":"ci.html","page":"CI","section":"","text":"CI Record locally, commit the cassettes, replay in CI with --record none : no API key, no model calls, the same result every run. # .github/workflows/e2e.yml name: e2e on: [push, pull_request] jobs: e2e: runs-on: ubuntu-latest steps: - uses: actions/checkout@v4 - uses: actions/setup-node@v4 with: { node-version: 24 } - run: npm ci - run: npx decisium install --with-deps - run: npx decisium run features/*.feature --record none --parallel auto --format junit:reports/junit.xml - if: failure() uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4 with: { name: decisium-runs, path: runs/ } runs/ holds the screenshots, Playwright trace and report.md of every failed scenario."},{"url":"ci.html#when-the-ui-changes","page":"CI","section":"When the UI changes","text":"CI fails as UI_CHANGED . If the change is intended, re-record locally and commit the cassette: decisium run features/campaign.feature --record new Optional, to collapse cassette diffs on GitHub: add *.cassette.json linguist-generated=true to .gitattributes ."},{"url":"ci.html#pin-an-ambiguous-target","page":"CI","section":"Pin an ambiguous target","text":"When an action fails as AMBIGUOUS , the report lists the candidates, each with a ready pin command. Check the screenshot, run the right one, replay: decisium pin features/campaign.feature:12 2 decisium run features/campaign.feature --record none Works for single-action Steps such as I click the \"Save\" button or I type \"Ada\" into the \"Name\" field ."},{"url":"ci.html#docker","page":"CI","section":"Docker","text":"docker run --rm --user \"$(id -u):$(id -g)\" -v \"$PWD:/work\" ghcr.io/andletenkov/decisium:<version> \\ run features/*.feature --record none Chromium is preinstalled. Use the version that recorded your cassettes; pass -e TYPESAFE_API_KEY to record."},{"url":"troubleshooting.html","page":"Troubleshooting","section":"","text":"Troubleshooting A failed run prints the reason under each Step and writes runs/<timestamp>/ : report.md (the Step, Jev's answers, the page text, a rerun command, ready for a coding agent), a screenshot, a Playwright trace and log.txt ."},{"url":"troubleshooting.html#outcomes","page":"Troubleshooting","section":"Outcomes","text":"Outcome Means Do ASSERTION_FAILED The app is wrong. Fix the app, not the Step. AMBIGUOUS The Step could mean more than one element. Quote the label or name the area, or pin a candidate. UNVERIFIABLE The check quotes nothing to compare. Quote the expected value. ELEMENT_NOT_FOUND Nothing matches the Step. Use the page's own label. BLOCKED The task cannot be done on this page. Check the start URL and earlier Steps; menus may need \"hover\". ACTION_FAILED The action did not take effect. Check the value's format (ISO for dates). STEP_TIMEOUT Too many actions for one Step. Split the Step, or raise maxTurns . UI_CHANGED A replayed Step no longer matches the page. Re-record with --record new if intended. PAGE_TOO_LARGE The page is over the model's limit. Test a narrower page or state. marginal pass Passed, but Jev was barely sure. Make the Step more specific. --strict fails it. check fails on a slow page The state came after the check gave up. Raise checkTimeout ."},{"url":"troubleshooting.html#a-step-passes-sometimes","page":"Troubleshooting","section":"A Step passes sometimes","text":"Live runs ask Jev each time; replays do not. Record once and run CI with --record none . If a live Step still wavers, reword it: I leave by the \"Search page\" link , not I leave for the search page ."},{"url":"troubleshooting.html#step-definitions-are-loaded-twice","page":"Troubleshooting","section":"\"Step definitions are loaded twice\"","text":"Your cucumber.mjs imports Decisium's steps and decisium run adds them again. Drop the import, or run npx cucumber-js instead."},{"url":"advanced.html","page":"Advanced","section":"","text":"Advanced"},{"url":"advanced.html#browser-context","page":"Advanced","section":"Browser context","text":"Tags on a feature or scenario set up its browser. @url:https://shop.example.com @locale:de-DE @timezone:Europe/Berlin Feature: Shop in German @viewport:iPhone-13 @geolocation:52.52,13.40 Scenario: Checkout on a phone When I add the \"Backpack\" to the cart Then the cart badge should show \"1\" @viewport: takes 390x844 or a Playwright device name (dashes for spaces). A scenario's tag wins over the feature's."},{"url":"advanced.html#client-steps","page":"Advanced","section":"Client steps","text":"Your own cucumber step definitions run next to Decisium: a line they match runs your code, every other line goes to Jev. Use them for setup the page cannot do (mocks, cookies, API login). // steps/campaigns.steps.ts import { Given } from \"@cucumber/cucumber\"; Given(\"the campaigns API returns {string}\", async function (name: string) { await this.context.route(\"**/api/campaigns\", (route) => route.fulfill({ json: [{ id: 1, name }] })); }); decisium run features/campaigns.feature --import steps/campaigns.steps.ts this.page is the current Playwright Page , this.context the BrowserContext . Client steps call no model and are not recorded."},{"url":"advanced.html#states","page":"Advanced","section":"States","text":"A reusable precondition, defined once in a *.state.feature file and used with @state: . # features/shop.state.feature @url:https://shop.example.com Feature: Shop states @state-def:logged-in @save:storage Scenario: Logged in When I log in as \"$USERNAME\" with password \"$PASSWORD\" Then the header should show \"Admin\" @state:logged-in Scenario: Checkout shows the total When I open the checkout Then the order total should be \"59.97\" @save:storage logs in once per run and reuses the cookies and localStorage . States can chain ( @state-def:cart @state:logged-in ). A failing state is a setup error, not a test failure."},{"url":"advanced.html#network-replay","page":"Advanced","section":"Network replay","text":"@replay-network:<glob> records matching browser requests and replays them, for a slow, costly or unstable backend (an app that calls an LLM). @replay-network:**/api/** Scenario: The assistant answers When I ask the assistant \"What is my balance?\" Then the answer should mention \"balance\" It follows --record like the cassette and is saved to <feature>.network/<scenario>.har ; commit it. WebSockets are not recorded."},{"url":"advanced.html#running-with-cucumber-js","page":"Advanced","section":"Running with cucumber-js","text":"decisium run already runs inside cucumber-js. To run Decisium Steps from plain npx cucumber-js (per-project install only): // cucumber.mjs export default { import: [\"node_modules/decisium/dist/steps.js\", \"steps/**/*.js\"], format: [\"decisium/formatter\"], worldParameters: { decisium: { record: \"none\" } }, };"},{"url":"advanced.html#agent-skill","page":"Advanced","section":"Agent skill","text":"A skill for coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, pi…): designs scenarios from app code or requirements, writes features and repairs failing Steps. npx skills add andletenkov/decisium It also ships in the package: $(npm root -g)/decisium/skills/decisium/SKILL.md ."}];
